  "description": "<div>\n  <p>A signal starts at vertex k and travels along directed links <code>[from, to, travelTime]</code>. All outgoing links forward the signal as soon as their source receives it. Return the first time by which every vertex has received the signal, or -1 if some vertex can never receive it.</p>\n  <p>Different routes can reach a vertex at different times. The final answer is the largest of the shortest arrival times.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> times = [[2,1,1],[2,3,1],[3,4,1]], n = 4, k = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Vertex 4 gets the signal through 3 after two time units.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> times = [[1,2,5],[1,3,2],[3,2,1]], n = 3, k = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Vertex 2 receives it in three units through 3, not five via the direct link.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> times = [[1,2,1]], n = 3, k = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> -1\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Vertex 3 is unreachable from 1.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 100</code>; vertices are numbered <code>1</code> through <code>n</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= times.length &lt;= 1000</code>; each link is <code>[u,v,w]</code> with <code>u != v</code> and <code>1 &lt;= w &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n    <li>At most one link exists for each ordered pair; <code>1 &lt;= k &lt;= n</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
